[gd_resource type="Theme" format=3 uid="uid://ccpt5srj6tnbv"]

; Deep Space theme — the project-wide default (project.godot gui/theme/custom).
;
; Two jobs:
;   1. BASE TYPES define what an unstyled control looks like. ~80 screens extend
;      plain Control and render nothing but these, so this is where app-wide look
;      actually lives. Radius is 4 everywhere; it used to be 8 here, 6 on inputs
;      and 4 in the Library's hand-built styleboxes, which is why a button's shape
;      told you which sprint built the screen.
;   2. TYPE VARIATIONS (the `X/base_type = &"Button"` entries) give semantic
;      variants a name. Per the Godot 4.6 theming guide, per-control overrides
;      "become hard to manage for shared custom looks" — variations are the
;      documented mechanism. A .tscn adopts one with a single theme_type_variation
;      property and no GDScript at all.
;
; Colours are the UIColors tokens (src/ui/components/base/UIColors.gd). Hover is
; lightened(0.15) and pressed darkened(0.15) of each variation's base colour, which
; is what DialogStyles computed at runtime before this file absorbed the job.

