; ── Tabs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; The app had NO tab styling at all: TabBar/TabContainer were absent from this
; file, so every tab rendered in Godot's stock grey. AdaptivePanelGroup builds a
; "PaneTabBar" for 16 screens and PrintSheetScreen builds one more, so these two
; entries are what makes tabs consistent everywhere at once. The selected tab is
; marked with a cyan underline rather than a filled pill — same accent language
; as the cards, and it survives long tab labels being clipped.

